####################################################################################################
# [1] HOW MATTER COUPLES -- the explicit coupling term, and WEP-exactness (eta = 0)
####################################################################################################

 The MI premise: INERTIA is rescaled (not gravity). In the action this is a UNIVERSAL kinematic
 dressing of the matter kinetic term by the frame scalar

       W[u,g] = s u^mu K(Box_u/a0^2) u_mu           (multiplies rho_m in S_matter)

 First-moment (quasistatic) closure -- the load-bearing bridge, u_mu Box_u u^mu = -|a|^2 on any
 timelike worldline (rederive_identity.py [I]; RE-DERIVED there 3 ways):

       W  -->  s (u.u) K(|a|^2/a0^2),   |a|^2 = a_mu a^mu,  a^mu = u^b grad_b u^mu  (4-acceleration).

 THE COUPLING IS:  matter is MINIMALLY coupled to the single metric g (rods, clocks, PHOTONS ride g),
 and modified inertia enters ONLY as the universal scalar dressing W of the inertial (matter-kinetic)
 term. It is NOT a disformal MATTER metric. Two consequences, both checkable:

 (1a) WEAK EQUIVALENCE PRINCIPLE. The inertial coefficient is mu_fw(|a|/a0)=K(|a|^2/a0^2), the
      SAME function for every body (no species index in W). So two bodies A,B at one point in
      the same external field g_bar get identical acceleration -> eta = |a_A-a_B|/a_avg = 0.
   [PASS] balance mu_fw(x) x = y solved by x = y*nu(y) (nested radical collapse 1+4x^2=(2y+1)^2, residual<1e-12 over y in [1e-2,1e2])
   [PASS] eta = (a_A - a_B)/a_avg = 0 EXACTLY (composition-independent; WEP exact, DERIVED)
      => WEP is EXACT (eta=0): the coupling carries no species label. DERIVED.

 (1b) MINIMAL, not a disformal MATTER metric. A disformal matter metric gM = g + C u_mu u_nu
      would ALSO be universal, but it would DRAG light (Maxwell built on gM) -> modify lensing
      in the matter sector and DOUBLE-COUNT the dynamics. The framework keeps photons on g and
      puts MI in the inertial SCALAR; lensing is handled separately by a light-only disformal
      PHOTON metric (MI_COMPLETION_WRITTEN_2026-07.md:45-49). Check: the Maxwell action is
      untouched by the scalar dressing (F_{mu nu} never contracts u), so photons see g exactly.
      Note: the MI dressing W = s u.K(Box_u).u is built only from (u,g); it contains NO F_ab,
      so the Maxwell/photon sector on g is literally untouched -> no light drag, no double count.
   [PASS] a disformal MATTER metric would instead DRAG light: O(C) Maxwell drag coeff != 0 (= cosh(3/5)/40) -> framework REJECTS it
      => coupling = UNIVERSAL inertial-scalar dressing, matter+light minimal on g. (DERIVED choice;
         the light-only disformal PHOTON metric carries lensing, separately.)

####################################################################################################
# [2] VARY THE FULL ACTION -- lambda, u (with constraint), and g_munu -> T_munu
####################################################################################################

 (2a) delta/delta lambda :  -(1/2)(u.u + 1) = 0   =>   u.u = -1   (unit-timelike constraint).
   [PASS] delta S/delta lambda gives the constraint u.u+1=0

 (2b) delta/delta u^mu (frame equation).  The ALGEBRAIC (non-derivative) part of the u-variation
      -- the part that could source the metric -- is strictly PARALLEL to u_mu (l=0):
        J_mu^alg = -[ rho s K(X) + lambda ] u_mu .
      Contracting with u^mu (and u.u=-1) fixes the multiplier:  lambda = -rho s K(X).
   [PASS] frame source is longitudinal: transverse projection h^a_mu J^mu = 0 (l=0, NO l=2 traceless-shear)
   [PASS] u^mu-projection: lambda = -rho s K(X) makes the algebraic source vanish  (algebraic, NO tertiary tower; constraint_structure.py)
      The remaining (derivative, K') terms are the WORLDLINE dynamics (accel a^mu, an l=1 vector);
      they never populate the l=2 traceless-shear whose divergence is AeST's Cassini Bianchi lock.
      => 'MOND does not force modified gravity' at the frame-equation level (MI_COMPLETION:31, sec4a). DERIVED.

 (2c) delta/delta g^munu -> T_munu (algebraic/leading part; passive u^mu upper = metric-free).
      Building blocks:  d(u.u)/dg^munu = -u_mu u_nu ,  d(a.a)/dg^munu = -a_mu a_nu ,
                        d sqrt(-g) -> +g_munu * L .   With L_matter = -(1/2) rho s (u.u) K(X):
      T_munu = alpha u_mu u_nu + beta g_munu + gamma a_mu a_nu ,  on-shell (u.u=-1):
         alpha = -rho*s*(sqrt(4*X + 1) - 1)/(2*sqrt(X))
         beta  = rho*s*(sqrt(4*X + 1) - 1)/(4*sqrt(X))
         gamma = rho*s*(sqrt(4*X + 1) - 1)/(4*X**(3/2)*a0**2*sqrt(4*X + 1))
   [PASS] PRINCIPAL limit K->1, K'->0 : anisotropic coeff gamma -> 0  => T_munu = alpha u u + beta g (fluid-like, Psi=Phi, NO slip; matches mi_lensing_from_stress_tensor.py, principal_symbol_blockdiag.py)
      The ONLY anisotropic (slip/enhancement-capable) stress is gamma a_mu a_nu, carried by K'(X):
      it is nonzero ONLY in the low-acceleration MOND/IR regime (K'!=0). This is exactly the open
      'enhancement' piece (lensing gap C) -- present in the tensor, magnitude = the curved solve.

####################################################################################################
# [3] CONSERVATION  grad_mu T^munu = 0  (Bianchi/Noether) + frame-constraint consistency
####################################################################################################

 THEOREM (diffeomorphism invariance). S_matter + S_u is a covariant scalar of (g, u, lambda, rho).
 Under x -> x + xi the identity delta S = 0 collects into the off-shell Noether/Bianchi relation

     grad_mu T^munu  =  -(E_u)_a (frame-eq terms)  -  E_lambda (constraint terms)  -  E_rho (continuity),

 so grad_mu T^munu = 0 ON-SHELL, i.e. when the u-equation, the lambda-constraint, and matter
 continuity all hold. The physically load-bearing fact (verified in [2b]): the u-equation IS
 imposed -- it fixes lambda -- and its source is l=0 (parallel to u), SOAKED by lambda. There is NO
 l=2 obstruction, so on-shell conservation is attained WITHOUT forcing a metric shear (no Cassini
 Bianchi lock). We verify the underlying Noether identity two ways.

 (3a) EXACT identity, generic field theory. For L(phi, d_mu phi) define the canonical tensor
      Theta^mu_nu = (dL/d(d_mu phi)) d_nu phi - delta^mu_nu L.  Then IDENTICALLY
      d_mu Theta^mu_nu = -(EL_phi) d_nu phi,   EL_phi = dL/dphi - d_mu(dL/d(d_mu phi)).
   [PASS] GENERIC Noether identity d_mu Theta^mu_x + (EL) d_x phi = 0  (holds for ANY L(phi,dphi))
      => on-shell (EL=0) the canonical stress tensor is conserved, for ANY Lagrangian of this
         form -- in particular the MI one below. (Hilbert T = canonical + Belinfante improvement,
         identically conserved, so grad_mu T^munu_Hilbert = 0 on-shell too.)

 (3b) INSTANTIATION with the MI acceleration kernel. Take the frame boost rapidity xi(t,x),
      u=(cosh xi, sinh xi, 0, 0) (unit-timelike identically), a^mu = u^b d_b u^mu, X=a.a/a0^2,
      L = (1/2) s rho0 K(X)  (the inertial dressing; rho0 const isolates the NOVEL sector).
   [PASS] MI-kernel Noether identity residual ~0 at 12 random (t,x) : max |resid| = 2.64e-16
      => the MI inertial dressing conserves its (canonical, hence Hilbert) stress tensor on-shell.
         The rho (dust) sector adds the standard perfect-fluid piece, conserved via continuity.

 (3c) FRAME-CONSTRAINT CONSISTENCY. u.u=-1 is preserved: its time derivative
      d/dtau(u.u)=2 u.a; on-shell u.a=0 (unit norm) => the constraint is dynamically stable.
   [PASS] u.a = 0 on the unit-norm surface => d/dtau(u.u)=0 (constraint preserved, no drift) : u.a = 0
   [PASS] lambda fixed ALGEBRAICALLY: Dirac 2nd-class block det = 4(u.u)^2 -> 4 on-shell (NO tertiary tower; constraint_structure.py / A10_dirac_block.py)
      => the passive frame stays passive under the matter coupling (0 propagating frame dof).

